   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Anima Base v1.0 text to image: a 2B anime and illustration model (not for photos). One switch turns on the Turbo LoRA for 8-step pictures. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: quality tags first (`masterpiece, best quality, score_7, safe,`), then tags and/or full sentences.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid. It is the authors' list plus `border, white border` (see Tips). It is ignored when Turbo is on (CFG 1).\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024, megapixels 2.25 = 1536x1536. The authors give 512x512 to 1536x1536 as the working range.\n   - **Turbo**: off = Anima Base with your **Steps** (30) and **CFG** (4). On = Turbo LoRA, 8 steps, CFG 1.\n   - **Seed**: a new one every run. Set \"control after generate\" to fixed to keep a picture.\n2. **Models**: the four loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change; the text comes from group 1.\n4. **Turbo switch**: three switches follow the **Turbo** input and pick the model, the steps and the CFG. The Turbo steps (8) and Turbo CFG (1) live here.\n5. **Sampling**: euler / simple, from the official template. More pictures per run: `batch_size` on the **Empty picture** node here.\n6. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/Anima/`.\n\n**What to expect:** 1024x1024 with Turbo off (30 steps, CFG 4): 21 to 23 s per picture on the test card. Turbo on (8 steps): about 4 s. 1536x1536: 60 s, Turbo 9 s. Turbo pictures have a stronger default style and thicker lines; Anima Base is plainer and follows style and artist tags more freely (the authors' description).\n\n**Prompt tips (from the model authors)**\n- Tags are lowercase with spaces, not underscores (only `score_7` style tags keep the underscore).\n- Tag order: quality / year / safety tags, then `1girl` / `1boy`, character, series, artist, everything else.\n- Artist tags need an @ in front: `@artist name`.\n- Full sentences work too: write at least two, very short prompts give random results.\n- Safety tags: `safe`, `sensitive`, `nsfw`, `explicit`. Put `safe` in the prompt to keep it clean.\n- It writes single words at best, not long text.\n\n**Tips from the test runs**\n- **White frame around the picture:** with the authors' negative prompt, 3 of 8 Anima Base pictures came out with a white border. With `border, white border` added (the default here) the same 3 pictures had none.\n- With Turbo on the negative prompt does nothing, so a frame can still appear: change the seed.\n- Other samplers: the authors like `er_sde` for Anima Base. One picture was made with it here and it was fine; the default stays the template's euler.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB · 64 GB RAM · ComfyUI 0.45.3. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
